# Lockpicking in a session. A minigame's first-time explanation pauses the game until clicked away, and a session keeps
# time running, so the minigame played on behind it: its fail bar ran out, the pick broke, and the explanation (read
# only on that click) came back the next time. Held while explained, the minigame waits for the player as alone.
# A lock one player opens is open for the other too (WorldObjects KindLock), without its lid opening.
# Hero 5 slot 0: B picks the archive trapdoor at (105,-410), which needs no talent, A the cellar port by the tavern.

include session.coop
A give misc_lockpick_simple 5
B give misc_lockpick_simple 5
A minigames on
B minigames on
B tp 105,-450
A tp -1272,-4640
B talent learn Talent_Lockpicking
A talent learn Talent_Lockpicking
sleep 3

# A player who never read the lockpick explanation: with it up, nothing runs out while they read.
B minigame unread Lockpicking
B use Interact_Port 300
B expect minigame contains explaining=1 timeout=3
sleep 6
B expect minigame contains "fail=0.00" timeout=1
B shot
B minigame read
B expect minigame contains explaining=0 timeout=2

# Won, and on the host too, then the locks are open.
B minigame win
B expect minigame == none timeout=5
B expect locks !contains "@105,-410" timeout=5
A use Interact_Port 300
A expect minigame contains open timeout=3
A minigame win
A expect minigame == none timeout=5
A expect locks !contains "@-1272,-4599" timeout=5
A shot

# Each finds the other's lock open in its own world.
A tp 105,-450
B tp -1272,-4640
A expect locks !contains "@105,-410" timeout=15
B expect locks !contains "@-1272,-4599" timeout=15
A expect counter worldapplied >= 1 timeout=5
B expect counter worldapplied >= 1 timeout=5
A shot
B shot
